 <marmarek@invisiblethingslab.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Jan 2016 01:53:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Log error code of EVTCHNOP_bind_pirq failure

Ease debugging of PCI passthrough problems.
---
 drivers/xen/events/events_base.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/xen/events/events_base.c b/drivers/xen/events/events_base.c
index 41309d38f78c..369b4c5d6a0d 100644
--- a/drivers/xen/events/events_base.c
+++ b/drivers/xen/events/events_base.c
@@ -867,7 +867,7 @@ static unsigned int __startup_pirq(struct irq_info *info)
 					BIND_PIRQ__WILL_SHARE : 0;
 	rc = HYPERVISOR_event_channel_op(EVTCHNOP_bind_pirq, &bind_pirq);
 	if (rc != 0) {
-		pr_warn("Failed to obtain physical IRQ %d\n", info->irq);
+		pr_warn("Failed to obtain physical IRQ %d (error %d)\n", info->irq, rc);
 		return 0;
 	}
 	evtchn = bind_pirq.port;
-- 
2.50.1

